  "worked_solution": "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\land$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\lor$\".\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $6 \\leq 3^2$ and $6$ is even. This corresponds to\n\\[\n\\underbrace{6 \\leq 3^2}_P \\quad \n\\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textbf{and}}_{\\land} \\quad \n\\underbrace{6 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is even} }_Q,\n\\]\nthat is, $P \\land Q.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $13$ is a prime number. This corresponds to $R.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\\[\n\\underbrace{6 \\leq 3^2 \\textbf{ and } 6 \\textrm{ is even } }_{P \\, \\land \\, Q}, \\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textbf{and}}_{\\land} \\quad \n\\underbrace{13 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is a prime number} }_R \n\\]\nthat is, $(P \\land Q) \\land R.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
