  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"questionExplanation-178524\" class=\"questionExplanation\" style=\"display: block;\"><p>The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\land$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\lor$\".</p>\n<p>Note that this sentence consists of two parts:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p><strong>Part 1:</strong> $6 \\leq 3^2$ and $6$ is even. This corresponds to\n\\[\n\\underbrace{6 \\leq 3^2}_P \\quad \n\\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textbf{and}}_{\\land} \\quad \n\\underbrace{6 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is even} }_Q,\n\\]\nthat is, $P \\land Q.$ </p>\n</li>\n<li><p><strong>Part 2:</strong> $13$ is a prime number. This corresponds to $R.$</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>So, we can express the sentence as\n\\[\n\\underbrace{6 \\leq 3^2 \\textbf{ and } 6 \\textrm{ is even } }_{P \\, \\land \\, Q}, \\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textbf{and}}_{\\land} \\quad \n\\underbrace{13 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is a prime number} }_R \n\\]\nthat is, $(P \\land Q) \\land R.$</p>\n<div class=\"studentAnswerHeader\">Your Answer:</div><div class=\"studentAnswer\">$(P \\lor Q) \\lor R$</div></div>",
